1. Literature Review Analysis 

Theme: Soft Computing & Multimodal Biometrics
Key Studies: Hussain et al. (2025); Rajakumar & Shanthi (2025); Chitrapu et al. (2026); Houssein et al. (2023)
Methods: CNN-LSTM, Multimodal CNN, Adaptive Focal Loss, Homomorphic Encryption
Key Findings: 98–100% accuracy; multimodal improves detection
Limitations: Adds complexity, cross-sensor issues, privacy concerns

Theme: Unsupervised & Deep Learning for Anti-Spoofing
Key Studies: Zhang et al. (2023); Kothadiya et al. (2023); Yook et al. (2024); Adami et al. (2024); Li & Ramachandra (2025)
Methods: ResNet, Transformer, Autoencoder, Attention Mechanism
Key Findings: Deep learning dominates PAD; unsupervised detects unseen attacks
Limitations: Generalisation to unseen attacks remains a challenge

Theme: Systematic Reviews & Emerging Challenges
Key Studies: Ametefe et al. (2024); Casula et al. (2024); Herke (2026); Li & Ramachandra (2025)
Methods: Literature Review, Comparative Analysis
Key Findings: No universal algorithm exists; puppet attacks remain underexplored
Limitations: Most studies lack real-world validation


2. Comparison of Existing Techniques

Approach: Traditional Handcrafted Features (LBP, HOG, GLDS)
Advantages: Simple, lightweight
Disadvantages: Poor generalisation to unseen attacks

Approach: Deep Learning (CNN, ResNet, Transformer)
Advantages: Learns complex patterns, high accuracy
Disadvantages: Requires large data, computationally expensive

Approach: Unsupervised Learning (Autoencoder)
Advantages: Detects unseen attacks without spoof samples
Disadvantages: Limited training data, cross-sensor issues

Approach: Multimodal Biometrics
Advantages: Improves accuracy and robustness
Disadvantages: Adds complexity, privacy concerns

Approach: Lightweight Models
Advantages: Suitable for edge devices
Disadvantages: May sacrifice accuracy


3. Research Gap Analysis

1. Limited availability of puppet attack datasets
   Evidence: Li et al. (2024) dataset has only 70 volunteers; lacks demographic diversity; accuracy drops on angled and side pressing

2. Variations in puppet attack conditions
   Evidence: Models trained on straight pressing only; fail on angled/side pressing (Li et al., 2024)

3. Limited cross-dataset and real-world evaluation
   Evidence: Most studies use controlled benchmarks (Ametefe et al., 2024); not tested on real-world conditions

4. Balance between detection performance and computational efficiency
   Evidence: Accurate models are computationally expensive; lightweight models sacrifice accuracy (Yook et al., 2024; Santos et al., 2024)


4. Summary of Methods/Algorithms Identified

CNN-LSTM: Hussain et al. (2025) - Fingerprint authentication
Multimodal CNN + Adaptive Focal Loss: Rajakumar & Shanthi (2025) - Liveness detection
MobileNetV2 + TAF + CKKS: Chitrapu et al. (2026) - Multimodal face-fingerprint system
LFLDNet (ResNet + Transformer): Zhang et al. (2023) - Lightweight fingerprint liveness detection
Sequential Attention + ResNet: Kothadiya et al. (2023) - Fingerprint PAD
Unsupervised Autoencoder + CBAM: Adami et al. (2024) - Unseen attack detection
LBP-HOG + SVM: Li et al. (2024) - Puppet attack detection


5. Relevant Datasets

LivDet (2017, 2019, 2023): Fingerprint liveness detection benchmark - PAD evaluation
FVC (2000, 2002, 2004): Fingerprint verification competition - Recognition and authentication
Puppet Attack Dataset (2024): 5,600 images, 70 volunteers - Puppet attack detection
CASIA-FingerV5: Multimodal face-fingerprint dataset - Multimodal biometrics
SOCOFing: Fingerprint dataset - Fingerprint recognition


6. Evaluation Metrics Identified

Accuracy: Classification performance
Precision: True positive rate
Recall: Sensitivity
F1-Score: Harmonic mean of precision and recall
EER (Equal Error Rate): Biometric authentication
FAR (False Acceptance Rate): Authentication systems
FRR (False Rejection Rate): Authentication systems
APCER (Attack Presentation Classification Error Rate): PAD evaluation
BPCER (Bonafide Presentation Classification Error Rate): PAD evaluation
ACER (Average Classification Error Rate): PAD evaluation


